From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 11:57:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] watchdog: qcom-wdt: add arm_on_probe module parameter

Some bootloaders (Google Pixel 2 XL) hand over with the watchdog
stopped, so a boot that dies before userspace waits for a human
forever. When arm_on_probe is set the driver arms the watchdog at
probe and reports WDOG_HW_RUNNING: the core then pings it only until
watchdog.open_timeout expires, after which an unclaimed watchdog
bites and "boot never finished" self-recovers into the bootloader's
retry path instead of hanging silently.

Default off, keeping stock behaviour unless both parameters are set
on the command line.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/watchdog/qcom-wdt.c | 13 ++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/watchdog/qcom-wdt.c b/drivers/watchdog/qcom-wdt.c
index 49bd04841f0c..883923ff5946 100644
--- a/drivers/watchdog/qcom-wdt.c
+++ b/drivers/watchdog/qcom-wdt.c
@@ -23,6 +23,17 @@ enum wdt_reg {
 
 #define QCOM_WDT_ENABLE		BIT(0)
 
+/*
+ * Some bootloaders (Pixel 2 XL) hand over with the watchdog stopped, so a
+ * boot that dies before userspace waits for a human forever. With this set
+ * the core pings the armed watchdog only until watchdog.open_timeout, then
+ * lets it bite: "boot never finished" becomes a reset instead of a brick.
+ */
+static bool arm_on_probe;
+module_param(arm_on_probe, bool, 0444);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(arm_on_probe,
+	"Arm the watchdog at probe even if the bootloader left it stopped (pair with watchdog.open_timeout)");
+
 static const u32 reg_offset_data_apcs_tmr[] = {
 	[WDT_RST] = 0x38,
 	[WDT_EN] = 0x40,
@@ -328,7 +339,7 @@ static int qcom_wdt_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	 * might use different ones and set running bit
 	 * to inform the WDT subsystem to ping the WDT
 	 */
-	if (qcom_wdt_is_running(&wdt->wdd)) {
+	if (qcom_wdt_is_running(&wdt->wdd) || arm_on_probe) {
 		qcom_wdt_start(&wdt->wdd);
 		set_bit(WDOG_HW_RUNNING, &wdt->wdd.status);
 	}
